WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:04.150
Hey, Julia, it’s Skyler
from Kelowna, BC, Canada.

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.670
Float would be a great place
for me at this stage in my career

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.610
because I thrive in a high-trust
and high-autonomy environment

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:13.570
where taking action, staying curious,
and saying the thing is celebrated.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.370
This is just how I operate.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:19.630
I’m always looking for new challenges,
feedback, new perspectives.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:24.190
I enjoy learning about, building,
and mastering software,

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.170
both inside and outside of the workplace.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.150
What drew me to Float?

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.890
Well, first it was the software.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:33.010
After researching it, I found
it to be interesting and impactful,

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.050
and something I would enjoy supporting.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.430
And then it went a little bit deeper,

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.470
and I started researching
the company as a whole.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:43.030
And I found that Float is a fiercely
transparent organization,

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.050
which excites me.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.990
I had the pleasure of reading
the public-facing handbook

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:51.730
and found that Float’s philosophies
and values aligned with me,

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:55.150
both on a professional and personal level.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:57.790
There’s many other things
I saw on that handbook

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.710
and in your hiring process
that excited me,

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.530
and I’d be happy to talk to you
about those more in the future.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:05.110
Thank you for your time,
and I hope to speak soon.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.160
Bye.
